course: dictionary
lesson: 3950
title: One word, two meanings: fungus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show which meaning you need. The dictionary gives two meanings for fungus. In «Germs include bacteria, viruses and fungi», the list tells you a fungus is a tiny living thing, like bacteria and viruses.
explain: In «Leave a slice of bread in a warm, damp place and in a few days fuzzy spots of mould appear», the fungus is the mould growing on the bread. Here the clues are fuzzy spots, bread and feeding, so fungus means a growth of mould on food.
explain: Fungus is a noun and its plural is fungi. Check the clues each time, because the same word can mean a living thing in one sentence and a growth of mould in the next.
fact: A fungus is a living thing that is neither a plant nor an animal.
fact: Mushrooms, toadstools, mould and yeast are all kinds of fungi.
fact: Yeast is a fungus that makes bread rise.
fact: Some fungi break down dead leaves and logs, which helps return nutrients to the soil.
fact: Never eat wild mushrooms, because some are deadly poisonous.
exercise: «Leave a slice of bread in a warm, damp place and in a few days fuzzy spots of mould appear.» What is the fungus in this sentence? | *The mould growing on the bread | The warm, damp place | The slice of bread before it was left out | The fuzzy spots of the sky
exercise: «Germs include bacteria, viruses and fungi.» Which of these is a fungus? | A carrot | A rock | *Yeast | A bee
exercise: Which word is the plural of fungus? | fungo | *fungi | fungis | fungas
test: «The southern corroboree frog almost disappeared because of chytrid fungus.» What harmed the frog? | *A chytrid fungus | Ants that it ate | Zoos | The mountains
test: «Fungus on the walls» means which? | A type of bird | *A growth of mould | A kind of plant with flowers | Something that gives out light
exam: Why should you never eat wild mushrooms? | They are too big to chew | They are only for birds | They taste bad | *Some are deadly poisonous
